OL,3,GNEWSAFresh drought measures to protect
OL,4,Adrinking water
OL,5,
OL,6,FSouth East Water is to reduce the daily
OL,7,Fvolume of water released into the River
OL,8,FOuse from the Ardingly Reservoir, which
OL,9,Fis just 17.1% full, to protect drinking
OL,10,Fsupplies.
OL,12,FThe Environment Agency (EA) declared a
OL,13,F"severe drought" in the parts of Sussex
OL,14,Fthe reservoir serves after the South
OL,15,FEast experienced its driest April to
OL,16,FSeptember in over a century.
OL,18,FIn order to protect drinking water in
OL,19,Fthe reservoir, South East Water will
OL,20,Freduce daily releases after the EA
OL,21,Fapproved an extension of its current
OL,22,Fdrought permit powers.
OL,23,APub: 22-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,330,320,200,140,0,100
